  "Notes": [
    {
      "Text": "Security update for libvirt",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "Summary"
    },
    {
      "Text": "This update for libvirt fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-18917: integer overflow in `NodeGetFreePages` RPC handler leads to heap buffer overflow and allows for\n  possible local privilege escalation (bsc#1275863).\n- CVE-2026-61477: newline injection in network XML DNS TXT/SRV fields allows for `dnsmasq` configuration directive\n  injection and can lead to arbitrary code execution as root (bsc#1274576).\n- CVE-2026-63622: symlink-following in `virFileChownFiles()` allows `swtpm` user to trick the root-level `libvirt`\n  daemon into changing the ownership of an arbitrary file and can lead to privilege escalation (bsc#1275264).\n- CVE-2026-63623: newly created volume images are temporarily world-readable during clone/convert operations, which can\n  lead to sensitive information disclosure (bsc#1275265).\n- CVE-2026-77159: root `chown()` on `swtpm` logfile follows symlinks and allows for root-owned file ownership changes,\n  which can lead to privilege escalation (bsc#1274946).\n",
      "Title": "Details",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
